{2}⁡x$ and $L({y}_{2})=3{cos}^{2}⁡x$ for some functions ${y}_{1}(x)$ and ${y}_{2}(x).$ What is $L(3{y}_{1}-{y}_{2})?$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186265816 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "bfd36b47-f530-50b4-b4b7-119c298890d2" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186265816 #edb/ref 1074 "For any linear differential operator,\n\n$$\nL(a{y}_{1}(x)+b{y}_{2}(x))=aL({y}_{1}(x))+bL({y}_{2}(x))\n$$\n\nwhere $a$ and $b$ are constants. \n\nIn our case, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L(3{y}_{1}-{y}_{2}) & =3L({y}_{1})-L({y}_{2}) \\\\  & =3\\cdot (2-{sin}^{2}⁡x)-3{cos}^{2}⁡x \\\\  & =6-3{sin}^{2}⁡x-3{cos}^{2}⁡x \\\\  & =6-3({sin}^{2}⁡x+{cos}^{2}⁡x) \\\\  & =6-3 \\\\  & =3.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186282438 #edb/ref 1080 "(24,26)" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186282438 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186282438 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "580c3843-6361-5a93-8e93-aa4eecc3f021" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186282606 #edb/ref 1080 "(\\frac{1}{16},-\\frac{7}{4})" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186282606 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186282606 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "6a91054f-adf7-5f56-83c2-fa3119dc478c" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186282871 #edb/ref 1080 "$(64,2)$ and $(\\frac{1}{16},-\\frac{7}{4})$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186282871 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186282871 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "88ea9708-0042-5422-b8c9-124b38c78848" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186282983 #edb/ref 1080 "(-9,-4)" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186282983 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186282983 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "95ec2ae6-b848-5b2c-9e73-71480e6476c7" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186283023 #edb/ref 1080 "(-7,-4)" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186283023 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186283023 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "9978da76-99f6-51aa-835d-d6470ba9b397" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186283395 #edb